Note: a to-do list bot. Every user has their own list, and the bot remembers it after a restart.

remember everything in "todo-memory.json".
set added to 0.

when someone sends "/start", reply "Send me any task to add it. Commands: /list, /done N, /clear.".

when someone sends "/list"
  if the number of items in their tasks is 0, reply "Nothing to do.".
  otherwise
    set their text to "Your tasks:".
    set their n to 0.
    for every task in their tasks
      add 1 to their n.
      set their text to their text and then a new line and then their n and then "." and then task.
    that's all.
    reply their text.
  that's all.
that's all.

when someone sends a message that starts with "/done"
  set their number to (the message with "/done" replaced by "") as a number.
  if their number is at least 1 and their number is at most the number of items in their tasks
    reply "Done:" and then item their number of their tasks.
    remove item their number from their tasks.
  otherwise reply "There is no task with that number.".
that's all.

when someone sends "/clear"
  set their tasks to an empty list.
  reply "Your list is empty now.".
that's all.

when someone sends anything else
  add the message to their tasks.
  add 1 to added.
  reply "Added. You have" and then the number of items in their tasks and then "tasks. All users added" and then added and then "so far.".
that's all.
